# Development

## Environment

`flake.nix` provides a dev shell with the toolchain from `rust-toolchain.toml`. With
direnv, `.envrc` loads it on `cd`; without, run `nix develop`. Personal environment
variables go in `.envrc.local`, which is ignored by git.

Nix flakes only see files tracked by git: `git add` a new file before Nix commands use
it.

`rust-toolchain.toml` is the single toolchain definition. rustup and Nix both read it;
change the channel or components there.

Without Nix, install Rust with [rustup](https://rustup.rs). It reads `rust-toolchain.toml`
and installs the same toolchain and components on first use.

## Project Layout
{% case layout %}{% when "bin" %}
```
{{project-name}}/
├── Cargo.toml   # Package manifest: metadata, dependencies, lints, profiles
└── src/
    └── main.rs  # Binary entry point
```

A single binary crate. Add modules as `src/<module>.rs` or `src/<module>/mod.rs`.
{% when "lib" %}
```
{{project-name}}/
├── Cargo.toml  # Package manifest: metadata, dependencies, lints, profiles
└── src/
    └── lib.rs  # Crate root and public API surface
```

A single library crate. Everything reachable from `lib.rs` is public API — see
[Documentation](code-style.md#documentation).
{% when "workspace" %}
```
{{project-name}}/
├── Cargo.toml  # Workspace root: shared metadata, dependencies, lints, profiles
└── crates/
    ├── {{project-name}}/
    │   ├── Cargo.toml
    │   └── src/main.rs
    └── {{project-name}}-core/
        ├── Cargo.toml
        └── src/lib.rs
```

A Cargo workspace with a binary crate, `{{project-name}}`, and a library crate,
`{{project-name}}-core`. Members live under `crates/` and are picked up by the
`crates/*` glob, so a new crate needs no edit to the root manifest.
{% when "members" %}
```
{{project-name}}/
├── Cargo.toml  # Workspace root: shared metadata, dependencies, lints, profiles
├── {{project-name}}/
│   ├── Cargo.toml
│   └── src/main.rs
└── {{project-name}}-core/
    ├── Cargo.toml
    └── src/lib.rs
```

A Cargo workspace with a binary crate, `{{project-name}}`, and a library crate,
`{{project-name}}-core`. Its members sit at the repository root. A new crate MUST be
added to `workspace.members` in the root `Cargo.toml`; there is no glob.
{% when "lib-workspace" %}
```
{{project-name}}/
├── Cargo.toml  # Workspace root: shared metadata, dependencies, lints, profiles
└── crates/
    └── {{project-name}}/
        ├── Cargo.toml
        └── src/lib.rs  # Crate root and public API surface
```

A Cargo workspace with one library crate, `{{project-name}}`. Members live under
`crates/` and are picked up by the `crates/*` glob, so a new crate needs no edit to the
root manifest. Everything reachable from a crate's `lib.rs` is public API — see
[Documentation](code-style.md#documentation).
{% endcase %}{% if is_workspace %}
### Workspace Rules
{% if has_bin %}
- Logic belongs in `{{project-name}}-core`, where it is testable and documented as a
  library. `{{project-name}}` stays thin: argument parsing, logging setup, and output.{% endif %}
- Shared metadata lives in `[workspace.package]`. Members MUST inherit it with
  `version.workspace = true`, `edition.workspace = true`, and so on. Only `name`
  and `description` are set per crate.
- Lints live in `[workspace.lints]`. Every member MUST opt in with:

  ```toml
  [lints]
  workspace = true
  ```

- Dependencies shared by more than one member SHOULD be declared in
  `[workspace.dependencies]` and referenced with `dep.workspace = true`.
- `{{lib_name}}` is declared there with its path and version, so a member that uses it
  adds `{{lib_name}}.workspace = true`.
{% endif %}
## Build and Run

```bash
cargo build                 # Build (debug)
cargo build --release       # Build (release, optimized)
{% if layout == "lib" %}cargo check                 # Check without building
cargo doc --open            # Build and open the API docs
{% elsif layout == "lib-workspace" %}cargo check --workspace     # Check without building
cargo doc --open            # Build and open the API docs
{% elsif is_workspace %}cargo check --workspace     # Check without building
cargo doc --open            # Build and open the API docs

# Run the binary
cargo run -p {{project-name}}

# Run with info-level logging
RUST_LOG=info cargo run -p {{project-name}}
{% else %}cargo run                   # Run the binary
RUST_LOG=info cargo run     # Run with info-level logging
cargo check                 # Check without building
{% endif %}```
{%- if has_bin %}

Logging goes to stderr through `env_logger`, initialized at the top of `main`. Only
errors print by default; `RUST_LOG` raises the level (`debug`, `info`, ...) or filters by
module (`RUST_LOG={{crate_name}}=debug`).

Nix builds the binary from a clean copy of the sources:

```bash
nix build                   # Build the binary into ./result
nix run                     # Build and run it
```

`nix build` reads `Cargo.lock`. Commit it, and run `cargo build` once first in a new
checkout that lacks it.
{%- endif %}

## Testing

```bash
cargo test                    # Run all tests{% if is_workspace %}, every member{% endif %}
cargo test test_name          # Run a single test by name
cargo test module_name::      # Run tests in a specific module
cargo test -- --nocapture     # Run tests with output
cargo test --lib              # Run only unit tests (no integration tests){% if has_lib %}
cargo test --doc              # Run only doc-comment examples{% endif %}{% if is_workspace %}

# Run tests for a single crate
cargo test -p {{lib_name}}{% endif %}
```

## Continuous Integration

`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs on every push to `main` and every pull request. Its
actions are pinned to commits; Dependabot keeps the pins current.

- **Detect code changes**: diffs the change against its base. When every changed file is
  one that cannot affect the build (Markdown, `docs/`, `LICENSE`, the issue templates,
  `.github/release.yml`), the jobs below are skipped.
- **check**: formatting, clippy, tests, and `cargo doc` with warnings denied
- **msrv**: `cargo check` with the oldest Rust allowed by `rust-version` in {% if is_workspace %}the root
  `Cargo.toml`{% else %}`Cargo.toml`{% endif %}
- **deny**: `cargo deny check` against `deny.toml` (licenses, advisories, sources)
- **CI passed**: fails if any job above failed. It is the check `main` requires before a
  pull request merges; see [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md#repository-settings).

A file type that can affect the build MUST NOT be added to the list in **Detect code
changes**. A Markdown file that becomes code, such as a README included as crate docs with
`#![doc = include_str!(...)]`, MUST be taken off it.

A weekly scheduled run checks everything and adds **latest-deps**, which runs
`cargo update` before testing to catch breakage from new dependency releases that
`Cargo.lock` hides. It is not part of **CI passed**. Dependabot opens
weekly update PRs for Cargo and GitHub Actions.

Raising `rust-version` is a deliberate change: dependencies that need a newer Rust fail
the **msrv** job until it is raised. A new dependency license that `deny.toml` does not
allow fails **deny**; add it to `licenses.allow` only after checking it.
